<title>FINLAND: INTERBANK 9-MTH OPERATING PROFIT RISES.</title>
<headline>INTERBANK 9-MTH OPERATING PROFIT RISES.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to end-Sept, 1996</p>
<p>				    (million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Net income from financial operations	21.2 vs 18.4</p>
<p> Other operating income			  28.9 vs 31.9</p>
<p> TOTAL INCOME					50.1 vs 50.3</p>
<p> Other expenses				    38.3 vs 34.7</p>
<p> Depreciation					 7.1 vs 5.9</p>
<p> Loan and guarantee losses			2.6 vs 8.1</p>
<p> Write-downs on securities			nil vs 0.7</p>
<p> OPERATING PROFIT AFTER CREDIT LOSSES	 2.1 vs 0.9</p>
<p> Extraordinary items		     charge 2.8 vs 0.1 gain</p>
<p> NET RESULT				    loss 0.7 vs 1.0 profit</p>
<p> Capital adequacy, percent		     17.3 vs 15.3</p>
<p>NOTES - Full name of the Finnish bank is Interbank</p>
<p>Osakepankki. It said it expected its 1996 operating profit to</p>
<p>develop in line with the trend in the interim report.</p>
<p>	    - Bank said it had swap contracts hedging its</p>
<p>low-yielding assets' interest rate risks which would give a</p>
<p>write-down of about three million markka if booked at market</p>
<p>value.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
</text>
